# Keeps an IDE's AI codebase indexer out of build output and the clients it is not looking at.
#
# Android Studio opens `clients/android` as the project, but Gemini's RAG crawler walks the whole
# checkout regardless — and "Mark Directory as Excluded" does NOT stop it (that writes
# `CidrRootsConfiguration/excludeRoots`, which only the native/CIDR roots read). This file is the
# control that actually applies. Syntax is .gitignore's.
#
# The episode that produced it: `clients/apple/Scripts/package.sh` staged a .dmg containing a
# symlink to the real /Applications and left it behind. The crawler followed it and indexed every
# installed app, Xcode's SDK included — 1,567,345 files scanned against a 176k-file repo, with the
# IDE unusable throughout. package.sh now removes its staging dir; this is the second line.

# Build output — large, generated, and worthless as context.
target/
clients/apple/build/
clients/apple/Packages/MailcalKit/.build/
clients/android/app/build/
clients/android/build/
clients/windows/**/bin/
clients/windows/**/obj/

# Sibling clients: real source, but not what an Android session is working on. Delete the line for
# whichever client you are actually in.
clients/apple/
clients/linux/
clients/windows/

# Agent scratch space. `.claude/worktrees/email-calendar-sync-engine` is a symlink to the engine
# checkout, so leaving this in drags a second repo into the index.
.claude/

# Captured artifacts — hundreds of PNGs, no text to index.
showcase-screenshots/
